        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Emtek 3311, Brisbane Mortise Entrance Handleset</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Brisbane Mortise Entrance Handleset has an F20 Mortise lock function which can be toggled to lock automatically upon closing the door. The Contemporary Brisbane Entrance Handleset will fit either 2-1/2 inch or 2-3/4 inch backsets and can accommodate doors from 1-3/4 inches to 2-3/4 inches thick. Choose from a huge selection of interior knobs and levers in a wide selection of the most modern finishes for a look that is all you. This Brisbane Mortise Handleset is available in dummy and single cylinder functions.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"2\">\r\n<tr>\r\n<td class=\"text\">\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Emtek Brisbane Handleset and the ANSI F20 Heavy Duty Lock Body:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Keyway: Schlage C</li> \r\n<li>UL 180 minute fire rating</li>\r\n<li>Deadlocking latch bolt with saw-proof inserts.</li>\r\n<li>Anti-pick security latch.</li>\r\n<li>When the deadbolt is engaged, the outside thumb press is automatically locked.</li>\r\n<li>The latch bolt is retracted by the thumb press / knob / lever on either side, except when the outside thumb press is locked by stop button, then it can only be opened from the exterior by use of the key. Making it ideal for doors you want to automatically lock. This feature can be easily toggled on and off by pressing the stop and release button on the mortise box face.</li>\r\n<li>Operating the interior trim retracts both the deadbolt and the latch bolt for emergency egress.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td align=\"right\">\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/EMT-F20-diagram.jpg?v=1704354539\" width=\"189\" height=\"255\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Emtek F20 Diagram\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> of the Emtek Brisbane Mortise Entrance Handleset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Material: Solid Brass</li>\r\n<li>Exterior Overall Height: 17-1/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Exterior Top Plate Width: 1-3/4</li>\r\n<li>Exterior Top Plate Height: 9-7/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Exterior Bottom Mount Width: 1-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Exterior Bottom Mount Height: 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Exterior and Interior Plate Thickness: 1/2\"</li>\r\n<li>Interior Height: 9-3/16\"</li>\r\n<li>Interior Width: 1-3/4\"</li> \r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-3/4\" - 2-3/4\" please specify</li>\r\n<li>Backset: either 2-1/2\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/EMT-3311-Specifications.pdf?v=1704262437\"><b>Emtek 3311 Specifications (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/EMT-F20-Mortise-Specifications.pdf?v=1704262243\"><b>Emtek ANSI F20 Mortise Box Specifications (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/EMT-F20-Mortise-Install.pdf?v=1704262243\"><b>Emtek ANSI F20 Mortise Installation Instructions (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Full Dummy Set:</b> Trim for non-working doors. It does not latch and does not lock. Usually used as matching trim for the non-working side of double doors.</li>\r\n<li><b>Single Cylinder:</b> From the exterior, a thumb piece operates the handleset latch and a key operates the deadbolt. From the inside, a thumbturn unlocks the deadbolt and a knob/lever operates the latch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<i>Sold Individually</i>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/EMT-3312-finish.jpg?v=1704354539\" width=\"514\" height=\"115\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Emtek 3312 Available Finishes\">\r\n</p>",
